<% content_for :title, "Kangxi radicals" %>

<% content_for :rightbar do %>
  <h3>View options</h3>
  <%= render "shared/view_options_rightbar" %>
<% end %>

<h1>Kangxi radicals</h1>

<p>
	Browse characters by Kangxi radical using Unihan <code>kRSUnicode</code>. 
</p>

<p>
	Kangxi Radicals (康熙部首) were first promulgated in 1615 by Mei Yingzuo 梅膺祚 in the dictionary Zihui 字彙. They are a system of categorisation for characters based on one of their visually prominent components; these are usually the semantic components that carry meaning. 
</p>

<p>
	Kangxi Radicals are not the same as Shuowen Jiezi's categories, which were more about shared graphical elements rather than a consistent broader set of strokes forming a semantically or phonetically meaningful component. 
</p>

<div class="kangxi-radicals-grid">
  <% @radicals.each do |r| %>
    <%= link_to "/dictionary/radicals/#{r.number}",
      class: "kangxi-radical-card",
      data: { turbo: false, turbo_prefetch: false } do %>

      <div class="kx-glyph"><%= r.radical %></div>
      <div class="kx-num"><%= r.number %></div>

    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<style>
  .kangxi-radicals-grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(84px, 1fr));
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .kangxi-radical-card{
    display:flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding: 10px 8px 8px 8px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.18);
    border-radius: 12px;
    text-decoration:none;
    min-height: 74px;
  }
  .kx-glyph{
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .kx-num{
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    opacity: 0.65;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
